    delphi:hasConfidence "0.95"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The period, location, proxy, and time window define a direct test. Public tree-ring archives have the necessary raw measurements and long chronology, while modern spectral methods can quantify uncertainty and distinguish periodicity from autocorrelated variability." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Construct Arizona ponderosa-pine ring-width chronologies for the stated interval, remove age trends, and test for a stable approximately 150-year spectral peak against red-noise and nonstationary alternatives. Compare the chronology with independent moisture and temperature reconstructions to identify the climatic correlate." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Only about three cycles occur in a 500-year window.", "Detrending and smoothing choices can create or suppress low-frequency peaks." .
